{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Human Oversight and Safeguards Use of AI for Asylum,  Vulnerability Seekers",
        "additional_details": "We want to stop the UK Government from using Artificial Intelligence as the main or only decision-maker in asylum claims, disability assessments, and vulnerability decisions for people with mental health conditions.\r\nAI can be unfair, biased, or inaccurate. We demand mandatory human review, clear explanations, and strong protections for vulnerable people. Human judgment must remain central.",
        "background": "\u2022  No AI as the sole decision-maker for asylum, disability or vulnerability cases\r\n\u2022  Mandatory human review for all AI-assisted decisions\r\n\u2022  Clear explanations for affected individuals\r\n\u2022  Strong safeguards for disabled people and those with mental health conditions\r\nFairness and human judgment",
